---
args: {"desk": "ReuseDesk", "exchange": "ReuseExchangeBook | null"}
returns: "ReuseExchangeReview"
---
1. Bind prior to exchange or ReuseExchangeBook { revision: 0, profiles: [], needs: [], concepts: [], legs: [], residuals: [], consumedEventIds: [] }. Bind profiles = qualifyOfferedMaterial(desk, prior.profiles). Bind needs = recoverFunctionalNeeds(desk.needs or an empty collection, desk.materialEvents). Treat the supplied prior offer as a source-bound hypothesis to update, never proof of unsupported properties.
2. Bind invalidatedLegIds to invalidateDependentTransfers(profiles, prior.legs) when an owner withdrew an offer or changed a transfer restriction, otherwise to []. Hold this entire dependent leg closure before confirming any package. Preserve actual in-transit custody and unknown external status for reconciliation.
3. For each relevant offer/need combination call inventQualifiedReuse(profile, need, desk.materialEvents), collecting its returned concepts. Bind qualifiedConcepts to only those returned concepts with qualified status and the required actual qualification evidence. Preserve multiple functional mechanisms and adaptations. Unknown maintenance history or essential suitability creates a qualification task; it cannot become an allocated match merely because the concept is creative.
4. Bind legs = planDependentExchangeLegs(qualifiedConcepts, profiles, needs, prior, desk.materialEvents). Require exact unit compatibility, evidenced density for weight/volume conversion, available quantities, real reservation receipts and permitted storage/transport windows before promising a transfer.
5. Bind residuals = reconcileRecipientAcceptance(legs, profiles, desk.transferReceipts or an empty collection, prior.residuals). Separate custody, title and recipient acceptance. A partial acceptance releases only its actually remaining quantity and preserves rejected-condition evidence.
6. Apply invalidatedLegIds to the corresponding legs before returning or proposing any transfer. Bind nextExchange as ReuseExchangeBook { revision: advance only for new source or transfer facts, profiles, needs, concepts: current concepts plus unaffected prior concepts, legs: current legs with the invalidation holds plus unaffected historical legs, residuals, consumedEventIds: prior IDs plus processed event/receipt identities once }. Return ReuseExchangeReview { exchange: nextExchange, qualificationTasks: unresolved material/suitability/conversion checks from profiles and concepts, proposedLegs: only currently eligible unexecuted legs, invalidatedLegIds, residualOffers: residuals, unmetNeeds: exact functional needs left unserved, outcomeClaims: only actual accepted quantities with custody/title/acceptance evidence }. Matching, reservation and dispatch alone do not establish completed reuse.
